# Cache Version Bumping Rule

Whenever you update JS and CSS related codes, you MUST bump the cache version parameter (e.g., `?v=XX`) in the HTML files (like `index.html`) where these assets are linked.
This ensures that users can view the latest changes without being served old, cached versions.

Use the `cache-version-bumper` skill or do it manually whenever you modify `*.js` or `*.css` files.

# Local Service Testing

When performing local service tests, note that the correct working URL is `http://127.0.0.1:8082` instead of `localhost:8082`.

# Plan Recording Rule

After finishing the implementation of any planned change (feature, bug fix, refactor), you MUST invoke the `plan-recorder` skill to record the finalized plan and verification steps into `docs/plans/` (preferred) or `.trae/documents/`.

# Hermes Bugfix Documentation Rule

After any Hermes-related bug fix (including Hermes routing, delegation, response parsing, or Hermes-driven chatbot behavior), you MUST add or update a markdown note in `docs/plans/` or `docs/troubleshooting_log.md`.
The note must include: symptom, root cause, files changed, and verification steps.
